bia minora and majora), or in the center crotch of your underwear.","Wear it for up to 20 minutes, up to 3 times a day, waiting at least 10 minutes between uses.","After each use, rinse with warm water, wash with mild soap, and air dry; wipe with 70% isopropyl alcohol at least daily. Replace the pod after 30 days or if damaged."],"sourceUrl":"https://hervpod.com/pages/usage-instructions","sourceLabel":"hervpod.com: Instructions for Use"},"warnings":["External use only. Do not insert into the vagina or anus, and do not ingest.","For temporary symptom relief only; it does not treat yeast infections, BV, or other conditions. See a doctor for itching or burning that doesn’t go away, unusual discharge, or odor.","Remove before urinating, and don’t flush it.","Don’t use with other silicone-based products.","If the pod ruptures, clean the skin and throw the pod away (the gel may be slippery)."],"ingredients":"Medical-grade silicone exterior with a gel interior (gel not disclosed). Drug-free; no active ingredients.","scientificCitations":[],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8094618/","text":"Local cooling for relieving pain from perineal trauma sustained during childbirth (Cochrane review, 2020)","summary":"A Cochrane review of 10 randomized trials (1,233 women) found that cooling with an ice pack or cold gel pad may reduce perineal pain in the first two days after birth, but the evidence is low to very low certainty. This is evidence for cold therapy in general, not for VPod specifically."},{"url":"https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/postpartum-pain-management","text":"ACOG: Postpartum Pain Management","summary":"ACOG recommends applying an ice pack or cold gel pack to the perineal area for 10 to 20 minutes at a time to relieve discomfort after birth. This is clinical guidance for cold therapy as a category, not validation of a specific product."},{"url":"https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/vulvovaginal-health","text":"ACOG: Vulvovaginal Health","summary":"ACOG suggests cold packs for perineal pain and advises seeing an ob-gyn for itching, burning, or swelling that doesn’t go away, since yeast infections, BV, and other causes need their own treatment. Cooling eases symptoms but doesn’t treat the cause.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"platform":"tiktok","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/tag/vpod","text":"TikTok: #vpod","summary":"TikTok posts tagged #vpod. The hashtag isn''t exclusive to this brand, so some posts may be about unrelated products; TikTok blocks automated access, so ayna hasn''t reviewed them."},{"platform":"walmart","url":"https://www.walmart.com/ip/VPOD-MULTI-3CT/19585123681","text":"Walmart: VPod Multi 3 Count","summary":"This 3-pack’s Walmart listing, with customer reviews. The site blocks automated access, so no rating is quoted here; read the reviews directly."},{"platform":"walmart","url":"https://www.walmart.com/ip/2-pack-VPod-Instant-Cooling-Relief-for-Vaginal-Discomfort-3-Cooling-Gel-Pods-for-Symptom-Relief/20452465708","text":"Walmart: 2-pack of VPod 3-pod boxes (6 pods)","summary":"A Walmart listing for two of these 3-pod boxes, with its own customer reviews. The site blocks automated access, so no rating is quoted here; read the reviews directly."},{"platform":"website","url":"https://hervpod.com/products/vpod-regular-multipack","text":"hervpod.com: VPod Everyday Comfort 3 Pack","summary":"VPod’s own product page."}]}},"integrations":[],"badges":[],"isEmergingBrand":false}'::jsonb),
  ('p-vpod-elite-single', 'VPod Postpartum & Menopause Comfort Single Pack', 'VPod', 'postpartum', 'physical', 'VPod’s extra-soft cooling gel pod designed for new moms, for targeted relief of tearing, bruising, swelling, dryness, and irritation before and after birth, and for menopause-related discomfort. Like the Everyday pod, you freeze it and place it in your underwear for up to 20 minutes; it has a 100% medical-grade silicone exterior and is drug-free. It eases symptoms but doesn’t treat their cause. One pod per pack; sold as VPod Elite.', '$21.99 (1 pod)', '/products/catalog/p-vpod-elite-single.webp', 'https://hervpod.com/products/vpod-elite-single-pack', '["discomfort","comfort","postpartum","pregnancy","menopause","external-only","reusable","hormone-free"]'::jsonb, '["vaginal-health","comfort"]'::jsonb, '["hervpod.com"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Registered with the FDA as an over-the-counter medical product, per hervpod.com. FDA registration means the company and product are listed with the FDA; it is not FDA clearance or approval.","materials":"Each pod is 3 in long x 2.5 in wide, with a 100% medical-grade silicone exterior and a flexible gel interior (the gel itself isn''t disclosed). Hypoallergenic, odor-free, and sterile when packaged. Made in China for Cool Comforts Co. (Cincinnati, OH).","recalls":"No recalls are mentioned on hervpod.com; check current FDA and manufacturer recall notices.","sideEffects":"Cold can feel too intense on sensitive skin, so VPod says to test the temperature first and limit each use to 20 minutes. Full warnings are listed below.","opinionAlerts":"hervpod.com contradicts itself on reuse: the product page says single-use and \"Do not reuse,\" but its FAQ and full instructions say the pod is reusable for up to 30 days with cleaning. ayna follows the detailed instructions; check the package insert."}'::jsonb, 'Cold therapy is a standard, low-risk way to ease vulvar and perineal soreness: ACOG recommends an ice pack or cold gel pack on the perineal area for 10 to 20 minutes at a time after birth, and a Cochrane review found cooling may reduce perineal pain in the first days postpartum (low-certainty evidence). VPod packages that idea as a curved silicone pod that stays in place in underwear.

Cooling only eases symptoms. It doesn''t treat yeast infections, BV, allergies, or menopause-related dryness, so it should be used alongside the right treatment, not instead of it. See a doctor for itching or burning that doesn''t go away, unusual discharge, or odor. VPod says it was developed with gynecologists; no study of VPod itself was found.', 'No customer reviews are shown on hervpod.com for this pack, and ayna didn’t find a retailer listing for the Elite single.', 'Cold therapy has category-level support for easing perineal pain (Cochrane; ACOG, linked below). No independent study of VPod was found, and cooling relieves symptoms only, not their underlying cause.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of ACOG guidance and a Cochrane review; not a direct clinician quote. Product details are from hervpod.com.', 'curated', false, false, null, false, '{"affiliateUrl":"https://collabs.shop/y6b4i1","faqUrl":"https://hervpod.com/pages/faq","doctorOpinionShort":"Cold packs are an ACOG-recommended way to ease perineal soreness, and a Cochrane review found cooling may reduce postpartum perineal pain. VPod relieves symptoms but doesn''t treat their cause. No study of VPod itself was found.","whoItsFor":["Prepartum and postpartum soreness, including perineal tears, episiotomy, bruising, and swelling","Menopause-related vulvar discomfort","Anyone wanting an extra-soft pod for very tender areas"],"howToUse":{"intro":"Per VPod''s full instructions:","steps":["Put the unopened foil pack in the freezer for at least 1 hour, until the pod feels stiff.","Take it out and let it rest 3 to 5 minutes, then wash your hands and open the pack.","Touch the pod gently to your vulva first to check the temperature is comfortable.","Place it between the inner and outer labia (labia minora and majora), or in the center crotch of your underwear.","Wear it for up to 20 minutes, up to 3 times a day, waiting at least 10 minutes between uses.","After each use, rinse with warm water, wash with mild soap, and air dry; wipe with 70% isopropyl alcohol at least daily. Replace the pod after 30 days or if damaged."],"sourceUrl":"https://hervpod.com/pages/usage-instructions","sourceLabel":"hervpod.com: Instructions for Use"},"warnings":["External use only. Do not insert into the vagina or anus, and do not ingest.","For temporary symptom relief only; it does not treat yeast infections, BV, or other conditions. See a doctor for itching or burning that doesn’t go away, unusual discharge, or odor.","Remove before urinating, and don’t flush it.","Don’t use with other silicone-based products.","If the pod ruptures, clean the skin and throw the pod away (the gel may be slippery)."],"ingredients":"Medical-grade silicone exterior with a gel interior (gel not disclosed). Drug-free; no active ingredients.","scientificCitations":[],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8094618/","text":"Local cooling for relieving pain from perineal trauma sustained during childbirth (Cochrane review, 2020)","summary":"A Cochrane review of 10 randomized trials (1,233 women) found that cooling with an ice pack or cold gel pad may reduce perineal pain in the first two days after birth, but the evidence is low to very low certainty. This is evidence for cold therapy in general, not for VPod specifically."},{"url":"https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/postpartum-pain-management","text":"ACOG: Postpartum Pain Management","summary":"ACOG recommends applying an ice pack or cold gel pack to the perineal area for 10 to 20 minutes at a time to relieve discomfort after birth. This is clinical guidance for cold therapy as a category, not validation of a specific product."},{"url":"https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/vulvovaginal-health","text":"ACOG: Vulvovaginal Health","summary":"ACOG suggests cold packs for perineal pain and advises seeing an ob-gyn for itching, burning, or swelling that doesn’t go away, since yeast infections, BV, and other causes need their own treatment. Cooling eases symptoms but doesn’t treat the cause.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"platform":"tiktok","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/tag/vpod","text":"TikTok: #vpod","summary":"TikTok posts tagged #vpod. The hashtag isn''t exclusive to this brand, so some posts may be about unrelated products; TikTok blocks automated access, so ayna hasn''t reviewed them."},{"platform":"website","url":"https://hervpod.com/products/vpod-elite-single-pack","text":"hervpod.com: VPod Postpartum & Menopause Comfort Single Pack","summary":"VPod’s own product page."}]}},"integrations":[],"badges":[],"isEmergingBrand":false}'::jsonb),
  ('p-vpod-elite-3-pack', 'VPod Postpartum & Menopause Comfort 3 Pack', 'VPod', 'postpartum', 'physical', 'VPod’s extra-soft cooling gel pod designed for new moms, for targeted relief of tearing, bruising, swelling, dryness, and irritation before and after birth, and for menopause-related discomfort. Like the Everyday pod, you freeze it and place it in your underwear for up to 20 minutes; it has a 100% medical-grade silicone exterior and is drug-free. It eases symptoms but doesn’t treat their cause. Three pods per pack; sold as VPod Elite.', '$55.99 (3 pods)', '/products/catalog/p-vpod-elite-3-pack.webp', 'https://hervpod.com/products/vpod-elite-multi-pack', '["discomfort","comfort","postpartum","pregnancy","menopause","external-only","reusable","hormone-free","cost"]'::jsonb, '["vaginal-health","comfort"]'::jsonb, '["hervpod.com","Walmart"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Registered with the FDA as an over-the-counter medical product, per hervpod.com. FDA registration means the company and product are listed with the FDA; it is not FDA clearance or approval.","materials":"Each pod is 3 in long x 2.5 in wide, with a 100% medical-grade silicone exterior and a flexible gel interior (the gel itself isn''t disclosed). Hypoallergenic, odor-free, and sterile when packaged. Made in China for Cool Comforts Co. (Cincinnati, OH).","recalls":"No recalls are mentioned on hervpod.com; check current FDA and manufacturer recall notices.","sideEffects":"Cold can feel too intense on sensitive skin, so VPod says to test the temperature first and limit each use to 20 minutes. Full warnings are listed below.","opinionAlerts":"hervpod.com contradicts itself on reuse: the product page says single-use and \"Do not reuse,\" but its FAQ and full instructions say the pod is reusable for up to 30 days with cleaning. ayna follows the detailed instructions; check the package insert."}'::jsonb, 'Cold therapy is a standard, low-risk way to ease vulvar and perineal soreness: ACOG recommends an ice pack or cold gel pack on the perineal area for 10 to 20 minutes at a time after birth, and a Cochrane review found cooling may reduce perineal pain in the first days postpartum (low-certainty evidence). VPod packages that idea as a curved silicone pod that stays in place in underwear.

Cooling only eases symptoms. It doesn''t treat yeast infections, BV, allergies, or menopause-related dryness, so it should be used alongside the right treatment, not instead of it. See a doctor for itching or burning that doesn''t go away, unusual discharge, or odor. VPod says it was developed with gynecologists; no study of VPod itself was found.', 'Customer reviews for this 3-pack are on its Walmart listing (linked below). Walmart blocks automated access, so ayna hasn’t pulled a rating; read them directly. hervpod.com shows no reviews on this pack’s page.', 'Cold therapy has category-level support for easing perineal pain (Cochrane; ACOG, linked below). No independent study of VPod was found, and cooling relieves symptoms only, not their underlying cause.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of ACOG guidance and a Cochrane review; not a direct clinician quote. Product details are from hervpod.com.', 'curated', false, false, null, false, '{"affiliateUrl":"https://collabs.shop/i776ti","faqUrl":"https://hervpod.com/pages/faq","doctorOpinionShort":"Cold packs are an ACOG-recommended way to ease perineal soreness, and a Cochrane review found cooling may reduce postpartum perineal pain. VPod relieves symptoms but doesn''t treat their cause. No study of VPod itself was found.","whoItsFor":["Prepartum and postpartum soreness, including perineal tears, episiotomy, bruising, and swelling","Menopause-related vulvar discomfort","Anyone wanting an extra-soft pod for very tender areas"],"howToUse":{"intro":"Per VPod''s full instructions:","steps":["Put the unopened foil pack in the freezer for at least 1 hour, until the pod feels stiff.","Take it out and let it rest 3 to 5 minutes, then wash your hands and open the pack.","Touch the pod gently to your vulva first to check the temperature is comfortable.","Place it between the inner and outer labia (labia minora and majora), or in the center crotch of your underwear.","Wear it for up to 20 minutes, up to 3 times a day, waiting at least 10 minutes between uses.","After each use, rinse with warm water, wash with mild soap, and air dry; wipe with 70% isopropyl alcohol at least daily. Replace the pod after 30 days or if damaged."],"sourceUrl":"https://hervpod.com/pages/usage-instructions","sourceLabel":"hervpod.com: Instructions for Use"},"warnings":["External use only. Do not insert into the vagina or anus, and do not ingest.","For temporary symptom relief only; it does not treat yeast infections, BV, or other conditions. See a doctor for itching or burning that doesn’t go away, unusual discharge, or odor.","Remove before urinating, and don’t flush it.","Don’t use with other silicone-based products.","If the pod ruptures, clean the skin and throw the pod away (the gel may be slippery)."],"ingredients":"Medical-grade silicone exterior with a gel interior (gel not disclosed). Drug-free; no active ingredients.","scientificCitations":[],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8094618/","text":"Local cooling for relieving pain from perineal trauma sustained during childbirth (Cochrane review, 2020)","summary":"A Cochrane review of 10 randomized trials (1,233 women) found that cooling with an ice pack or cold gel pad may reduce perineal pain in the first two days after birth, but the evidence is low to very low certainty. This is evidence for cold therapy in general, not for VPod specifically."},{"url":"https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/postpartum-pain-management","text":"ACOG: Postpartum Pain Management","summary":"ACOG recommends applying an ice pack or cold gel pack to the perineal area for 10 to 20 minutes at a time to relieve discomfort after birth. This is clinical guidance for cold therapy as a category, not validation of a specific product."},{"url":"https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/vulvovaginal-health","text":"ACOG: Vulvovaginal Health","summary":"ACOG suggests cold packs for perineal pain and advises seeing an ob-gyn for itching, burning, or swelling that doesn’t go away, since yeast infections, BV, and other causes need their own treatment. Cooling eases symptoms but doesn’t treat the cause.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"platform":"tiktok","url":"https://www.tiktok.com/tag/vpod","text":"TikTok: #vpod","summary":"TikTok posts tagged #vpod. The hashtag isn''t exclusive to this brand, so some posts may be about unrelated products; TikTok blocks automated access, so ayna hasn''t reviewed them."},{"platform":"walmart","url":"https://www.walmart.com/ip/Vpod-Elite-Multi-pack/19824372766","text":"Walmart: VPod Elite Multi-pack","summary":"This 3-pack’s Walmart listing, with customer reviews. The site blocks automated access, so no rating is quoted here; read the reviews directly."},{"platform":"website","url":"https://hervpod.com/products/vpod-elite-multi-pack","text":"hervpod.com: VPod Postpartum & Menopause Comfort 3 Pack","summary":"VPod’s own product page."}]}},"integrations":[],"badges":[],"isEmergingBrand":false}'::jsonb),
  ('d-soonr', 'Soonr: Fertility App for Couples', 'Soonr', 'tracker', 'digital', 'A preconception app built for both partners. Each person logs their own health habits (exercise, meals, supplements, symptoms, and habits they’re avoiding), and both see each other’s progress; consistent logging fills a shared "Momentum Orb." It also tracks periods, discharge, ovulation test results, and basal body temperature, predicts the fertile window, and can sync Apple Watch wrist temperature through Apple Health. For hormone readings, it pairs with the separately sold Surearly SMART test reader.', 'Free; Premium $12.99/month or $9.16/month billed yearly (launch price $5.50/month billed yearly)', '/products/soonr/soonr-app.png', 'https://apps.apple.com/us/app/soonr-fertility-for-couples/id6756647515', '["fertility","pregnancy","privacy"]'::jsonb, '["cycle-tracking","fertility"]'::jsonb, '["App Store","Google Play"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Not FDA-cleared. Soonr describes itself as a wellness tool, not medical advice.","materials":"N/A (app)","recalls":"N/A","allergens":"N/A","sideEffects":"N/A (software).","opinionAlerts":"Fertile-window predictions from period and symptom logs are estimates; Soonr suggests the Surearly SMART reader for actual hormone readings. The app is new (App Store release February 2026), so there’s little long-term user feedback yet."}'::jsonb, 'Soonr’s focus on both partners matches clinical advice: ACOG’s prepregnancy guidance covers diet and a prenatal vitamin with folic acid, exercise, a healthy weight, and cutting out tobacco and alcohol, and partners’ habits matter too. An app that makes those habits shared and visible may help couples stay consistent, though no study of Soonr itself was found.

For timing, fertile-window predictions based on period logs are estimates. Urine LH testing is better supported: a 2023 Cochrane review found timing sex with ovulation tests probably improves pregnancy and live-birth rates, which is why pairing the app with a test reader can help. ACOG recommends a fertility evaluation after 1 year of trying, or 6 months if you’re over 35.', 'On the App Store, Soonr has a 4.7-star average from 21 ratings (as of September 30, 2026), a small number since the app launched in February 2026. Read the reviews directly on the App Store and Google Play listings linked below.', 'No independent study of the Soonr app was found. Its fertile-window predictions are estimates; urine ovulation testing, which it can log and sync, has moderate-quality Cochrane evidence for improving pregnancy rates.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of ACOG guidance and a Cochrane review; not a direct clinician quote. App details are from soonr.health, its App Store listing, and its privacy policy.', 'curated', false, false, 4.7, true, '{"userRatingSourceUrl":"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/soonr-fertility-for-couples/id6756647515","platform":"iOS, Android","website":"https://soonr.health/","whereToBuyLinks":{"App Store":"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/soonr-fertility-for-couples/id6756647515","Google Play":"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.health.soonr"},"privacy":{"dataStorage":"AWS servers in the United States and other countries, per Soonr’s privacy policy. Operated by Vespexx Inc.","sellsData":"Says it does not sell personal data or share it for cross-context behavioral advertising.","hipaa":"Not described as HIPAA-covered; consumer wellness app.","keyPolicy":"Health data is shared with a connected partner only with your explicit consent, and disconnecting removes previously shared data from the partner’s app."},"doctorOpinionShort":"A couples’ preconception tracker built around ACOG-style healthy habits for both partners. Fertile-window predictions are estimates; pairing it with LH testing, which Cochrane evidence supports, is more precise. No study of the app itself was found.","whoItsFor":["Couples planning a pregnancy who want to work on health habits together","Partners who want to see each other’s cycle calendar, fertile window, and daily logs","Anyone who wants to log ovulation tests and BBT alongside lifestyle habits"],"howToUse":{"intro":"Per Soonr’s own getting-started steps:","steps":["Download the app and answer a few questions about your health, lifestyle, and goals.","Invite your partner with a link; you both agree on what health data is shared.","Log daily health factors (exercise, meals, symptoms, supplements, habits) in about 5 minutes a day.","Track your cycle; Soonr predicts the fertile window and shows it on a shared calendar.","Optional: connect the Surearly SMART reader (sold separately) for LH and progesterone-marker readings."],"sourceUrl":"https://soonr.health/","sourceLabel":"soonr.health"},"warnings":["Soonr is a wellness tool, not medical advice or a diagnosis.","Not a form of birth control.","See a clinician if you haven’t conceived after 1 year of trying (6 months if you’re over 35), per ACOG."],"integrations":["Apple Health","Surearly SMART"],"badges":[],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10501857/","text":"Timed intercourse for couples trying to conceive (Cochrane review, 2023)","summary":"A Cochrane review of 7 randomized trials (2,464 women or couples) found that timing sex with urine ovulation (LH) tests probably increases the chance of pregnancy and live birth compared with not predicting ovulation (moderate-quality evidence). This supports ovulation testing in general, not a specific device or app."},{"url":"https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/good-health-before-pregnancy-prepregnancy-care","text":"ACOG: Good Health Before Pregnancy (Prepregnancy Care)","summary":"ACOG recommends steps before pregnancy such as a healthy diet and prenatal vitamin with folic acid, regular exercise, reaching a healthy weight, and stopping tobacco, alcohol, and other substances, and notes partners shouldn’t smoke around you. These are the kinds of habits the Soonr app tracks; this is general guidance, not validation of the app."},{"url":"https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/evaluating-infertility","text":"ACOG: Evaluating Infertility","summary":"ACOG explains that urine tests detect the rise in luteinizing hormone (LH) that comes before ovulation, and recommends a fertility evaluation after 1 year of trying (or 6 months if you’re over 35). This is clinical guidance for the category, not validation of a specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"url":"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/soonr-fertility-for-couples/id6756647515","text":"App Store: Soonr: Fertility for Couples","summary":"The app’s App Store listing: 4.7 stars from 21 ratings as of September 30, 2026."},{"url":"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.health.soonr","text":"Google Play: Soonr","summary":"The app’s Google Play listing, with Android user reviews."},{"url":"https://soonr.health/","text":"soonr.health","summary":"Soonr’s own site, with features and pricing."}]}},"isEmergingBrand":false}'::jsonb),
  ('p-surearly-smart-ovulation-test', 'Surearly SMART Ovulation Test Reader (works with Soonr)', 'Surearly', 'diagnostics', 'physical', 'A digital at-home urine test reader that measures two hormones from one stick: LH, whose surge predicts your fertile window, and P3G (a progesterone marker, also called PdG), which confirms ovulation happened. Results appear on the reader in about 5 minutes and sync by Bluetooth to the Soonr app (or Surearly’s own app), where you can see hormone trends across cycles and share them with a partner. Comes with 20 test sticks. Made by Sugentech (Surearly); Soonr sells it as its recommended hormone tester.', 'See Amazon for current price (reader + 20 test sticks)', '/products/catalog/p-surearly-smart-ovulation-test.webp', 'https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H1BCL6NB?tag=aynahealth-20', '["fertility","pregnancy"]'::jsonb, '["fertility","cycle-tracking"]'::jsonb, '["Amazon"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Listed in the FDA’s device database (GUDID) as an over-the-counter LH test (product code NGE) made by Sugentech; no 510(k) clearance is listed. Soonr also describes it as CE-IVD marked.","materials":"Digital test reader with Bluetooth, plus 20 single-use urine test sticks. Detects LH at 10 mIU/mL or above and progesterone metabolite (P3G) at 5 µg/mL or above, per its FDA device listing.","recalls":"No recalls are listed in its FDA device record; check current FDA and manufacturer notices.","sideEffects":"None expected (urine test). Full notes are listed below.","opinionAlerts":"Accuracy figures (the box claims over 99% accuracy at detecting the LH surge) are the manufacturer’s. Surearly and Soonr are separate companies; Soonr promotes the device and its app syncs with it."}'::jsonb, 'Urine LH testing is one of the better-supported tools for trying to conceive: ACOG explains that these tests detect the LH rise before ovulation, and a 2023 Cochrane review found timing sex with ovulation tests probably increases pregnancy and live-birth rates (moderate-quality evidence). Adding a progesterone-marker (P3G/PdG) reading can help confirm that ovulation actually happened, which LH alone can’t show.

The reader’s digital result removes the guesswork of reading faint lines. No independent study of this specific reader was found, and ovulation tests can’t diagnose infertility; ACOG recommends an evaluation after 1 year of trying, or 6 months if you’re over 35.', 'Customer reviews for this reader are on its Amazon listing (linked below). Amazon blocks automated access, so ayna hasn’t pulled a rating; read them directly.', 'Urine LH testing probably improves pregnancy and live-birth rates when used to time sex (Cochrane 2023, moderate-quality evidence). No independent study of the Surearly SMART reader was found.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of ACOG guidance, a Cochrane review, and the device’s FDA listing; not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"doctorOpinionShort":"LH ovulation testing has moderate-quality Cochrane evidence for improving pregnancy rates, and adding a progesterone-marker reading helps confirm ovulation. No study of this specific reader was found.","whoItsFor":["People trying to conceive who want to pinpoint their fertile window","Anyone who wants to confirm ovulation happened, not just predict it","Soonr app users who want real hormone readings synced to their shared calendar"],"howToUse":{"intro":"Per Soonr and the device’s FDA listing:","steps":["Insert a test stick into the reader and apply urine as directed on the package insert.","Read the result on the reader in about 5 minutes.","Results sync by Bluetooth to the Soonr app (or the Surearly SMART app), where you can track LH and P3G across cycles."],"sourceUrl":"https://soonr.health/","sourceLabel":"soonr.health: Surearly SMART"},"warnings":["Follow the package insert for when in your cycle to start testing and what time of day to test.","Ovulation tests predict and confirm ovulation; they can’t diagnose infertility or confirm pregnancy.","See a clinician if you haven’t conceived after 1 year of trying (6 months if you’re over 35), per ACOG."],"integrations":["Soonr","Surearly SMART app"],"badges":[],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10501857/","text":"Timed intercourse for couples trying to conceive (Cochrane review, 2023)","summary":"A Cochrane review of 7 randomized trials (2,464 women or couples) found that timing sex with urine ovulation (LH) tests probably increases the chance of pregnancy and live birth compared with not predicting ovulation (moderate-quality evidence). This supports ovulation testing in general, not a specific device or app."},{"url":"https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/evaluating-infertility","text":"ACOG: Evaluating Infertility","summary":"ACOG explains that urine tests detect the rise in luteinizing hormone (LH) that comes before ovulation, and recommends a fertility evaluation after 1 year of trying (or 6 months if you’re over 35). This is clinical guidance for the category, not validation of a specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"platform":"amazon","url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0H1BCL6NB","text":"Amazon: Surearly Digital Fertility Monitor, LH + PdG Ovulation Tracker with App","summary":"This reader’s Amazon listing (reader + 20 test sticks), with customer reviews. Amazon blocks automated access, so no rating is quoted here; read the reviews directly."},{"url":"https://accessgudid.nlm.nih.gov/devices/08809408863482","text":"FDA device listing (GUDID): Surearly SMART Ovulation Test","summary":"The device’s entry in the FDA/NIH device database: over-the-counter LH test by Sugentech, in commercial distribution."}]}},"isEmergingBrand":false}'::jsonb),
  ('p-resa-rhythm-bracelet', 'Rèsa Rhythm Bracelet', 'Rèsa', 'tracker', 'physical', 'Rèsa is an 18K gold-plated bracelet that doubles as a wellness wearable built for female physiology. It continuously tracks heart-rate variability, resting heart rate, skin temperature, sleep, respiration and activity, combines that with your cycle information, and reads it against your personal baseline to make sense of three rhythms at once: hormonal, circadian and stress. Instead of scores, the Rèsa app gives one plain-language read and one suggestion for the day, then checks in on whether it helped.', '$9.90 waitlist deposit', '/products/resa/rhythm-bracelet.webp', 'https://www.resa-labs.com/', '["resa","wearable","jewelry","waitlist","pre-launch","sleep","stress","hrv","cycle","irregular","privacy"]'::jsonb, '["cycle-tracking","fitness-cycle"]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Consumer wellness wearable, not a medical device; not FDA-cleared, and not intended to diagnose or treat any condition.","materials":"18K gold-plated bracelet, about 15g, 100% waterproof, roughly 7 days of battery per charge, per the brand.","recalls":"Not yet released, no recalls.","sideEffects":"None expected from wearing it. As with any metal jewelry, people with plating or metal sensitivities should check final material details at launch."}'::jsonb, 'HRV, resting heart rate, skin temperature and sleep are well-established wearable signals, and skin and wrist temperature in particular track the post-ovulation temperature shift across the menstrual cycle. Rèsa''s pitch is interpreting those signals together, against your own baseline, instead of one metric at a time. The device has not launched, so there is no published validation of its accuracy or of its hormone-trend ("Hormone Rhythm") estimates yet. Its scientific advisory board includes Prof. Tory Eisenlohr-Moul (hormone, mood and autonomic research), Prof. Sarah E. Hill (Texas Christian University, reproductive hormone neuroscience) and Dr. Daniela Avila-Varela (Universitat Pompeu Fabra, menstrual-cycle brain dynamics), per the brand.', null, 'No study of Rèsa exists yet because it hasn''t launched, so this is evidence for wrist wearables in general. In a 2019 study of a different bracelet (Ava) in 193 women, wrist skin temperature, heart rate, and breathing rate all shifted with cycle phase, and the company''s algorithm picked out the fertile window with about 90% accuracy in women who wore it consistently; several authors worked for the company. A 2021 study of the same bracelet in 57 women found wrist temperature caught ovulation more often than a morning oral thermometer (62% vs 23%) but gave many more false alarms.', 'brand', 'Sourced from Rèsa''s own site and product-intro materials, not independent clinical literature.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"prelaunch":true,"waitlistCtaLabel":"Join waitlist · $9.90 deposit","affiliateUrl":"https://shop.resa-labs.com/?utm_source=ayna_partner&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=market_test","doctorOpinionShort":"A promising idea built on established wearable signals, but pre-launch, so its accuracy and hormone-trend estimates are not yet validated.","whoItsFor":["People who want wearable insight into how their cycle, sleep and stress interact, without wearing something that looks like a fitness tracker","Early adopters comfortable reserving a product before it ships","Not a substitute for clinical cycle, fertility or hormone testing"],"warnings":["Pre-launch: specs, final price and ship date are not final.","Wellness insights only. It is not contraception and does not diagnose hormonal conditions."],"scientificCitations":[{"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33526880/","text":"Pierson et al. Daily, weekly, seasonal and menstrual cycles in women''s mood, behaviour and vital signs. Nature Human Behaviour (2021)","summary":"Analyzed 241 million observations from 3.3 million women in 109 countries using the Clue period-tracking app. Of the daily, weekly, seasonal and menstrual cycles, the menstrual cycle had the largest effect on most measures of mood, behaviour and vital signs, while sleep and exercise stayed more constant."},{"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11666598/","text":"Jasinski et al. A novel method for quantifying fluctuations in wearable-derived daily cardiovascular parameters across the menstrual cycle. npj Digital Medicine (2024)","summary":"Wearable data from 11,590 people across 45,811 menstrual cycles. Resting heart rate and HRV rose and fell in a regular pattern through the cycle: resting heart rate lowest and HRV highest around day 5, resting heart rate highest around day 26 and HRV lowest around day 27. The swing was smaller in older participants and those using birth control."},{"url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7141121/","text":"Schmalenberger et al. Menstrual cycle changes in vagally-mediated heart rate variability are associated with progesterone. Journal of Clinical Medicine (2020)","summary":"Two within-person studies that measured hormones and HRV repeatedly across the cycle. Higher-than-usual progesterone predicted lower-than-usual HRV, and HRV was lowest in the mid-luteal phase; estradiol showed no significant effect. A practical example of why the same HRV number can mean different things depending on cycle phase."},{"url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38767963/","text":"Gombert-Labedens et al. Using wearable skin temperature data to advance tracking and characterization of the menstrual cycle in a real-world setting. Journal of Biological Rhythms (2024)","summary":"Minute-by-minute wearable skin temperature from 120 women over a menstrual cycle. Temperature across the cycle was better described as a smooth rhythm (a cosinor model) than as a simple two-phase low/high step, which lets wearables measure the cycle''s temperature rhythm in everyday life."}],"integrations":[],"badges":["Pre-launch","Waitlist","Female-Founded"],"isEmergingBrand":true,"researchScienceSources":[{"url":"https://jmir.org/2019/4/e13404/","label":"Goodale et al., Journal of Medical Internet Research 2019: Wearable sensors reveal menses-driven changes in physiology","summary":"Found wrist temperature, heart rate, and breathing rate change across the menstrual cycle in a wrist wearable, with a disclosed company conflict of interest."},{"url":"https://www.jmir.org/2021/6/e20710/","label":"Zhu et al., Journal of Medical Internet Research 2021: Accuracy of wrist skin temperature in detecting ovulation","summary":"Found wrist skin temperature during sleep was more sensitive but less specific than basal body temperature for detecting ovulation."}],"researchFilled":["effectiveness"]}'::jsonb),
  ('p-advil-ibuprofen-200', 'Advil Ibuprofen 200 mg Tablets', 'Advil', 'medication', 'physical', 'Over-the-counter ibuprofen 200 mg, an NSAID pain reliever. The label lists menstrual cramps among its uses, along with headache, backache, muscle aches and fever. Adults take 1 tablet every 4 to 6 hours (2 if 1 does not help), and no more than 6 in 24 hours unless a doctor says otherwise.', '$23.49 for 300 tablets at Target (also sold in 20, 24, 100 and 200 counts)', 'https://target.scene7.com/is/image/Target/GUEST_0ffb5fb8-4373-4132-85cd-ff831395c45f', 'https://www.target.com/p/advil-pain-reliever-fever-reducer-tablets-ibuprofen-nsaid/-/A-15772219', '["cramps","endometriosis","discomfort","cost"]'::jsonb, '["cramp-relief"]'::jsonb, '["Target"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"FDA-regulated over-the-counter drug with a Drug Facts label (DailyMed, Haleon US Holdings LLC).","materials":"Coated oral tablet.","recalls":"No recalls found on the pages reviewed.","allergens":"Ibuprofen may cause a severe allergic reaction, especially in people allergic to aspirin. Do not use if you have had an allergic reaction to any other pain reliever or fever reducer.","sideEffects":"The label warns that NSAIDs can cause severe stomach bleeding and that NSAIDs (except aspirin) increase the risk of heart attack, heart failure and stroke, with higher risk at higher doses or longer use. Take with food or milk if it upsets your stomach.","opinionAlerts":"Avoid at 20 weeks of pregnancy or later unless a doctor directs it. Ibuprofen may reduce the heart protection of daily aspirin."}'::jsonb, 'MedlinePlus lists NSAIDs such as ibuprofen as a first step for period pain, taken when symptoms start or when your period begins and continued for a few days. They are not right for everyone: skip them if you have ulcers or other stomach problems, bleeding problems or liver disease, or a true aspirin allergy. See a clinician if NSAIDs and self-care do not help, cramps suddenly get worse, or you have pain when you are not on your period. This is guidance about ibuprofen as a medicine, not a test of this brand.', 'Target shows a 4.69 out of 5 rating from 12,462 reviews for this Advil tablet listing.', 'Ibuprofen is an NSAID that clinical sources such as MedlinePlus recommend for menstrual cramps. Evidence is for the ingredient in general and does not validate this brand over generic ibuprofen 200 mg, which has the same active ingredient.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of peer-reviewed literature and clinical guidance. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"communityReviewSourceUrl":"https://www.target.com/p/advil-pain-reliever-fever-reducer-tablets-ibuprofen-nsaid/-/A-15772219","communityReviewSourceLabel":"Target reviews","ingredients":"Active: ibuprofen 200 mg (NSAID) per tablet. Inactive ingredients vary by Advil format; see the DailyMed label.","warnings":["Allergy alert: ibuprofen may cause a severe allergic reaction, especially in people allergic to aspirin.","Stomach bleeding warning: risk is higher if you are 60 or older, have had ulcers or bleeding problems, take a blood thinner or steroid, take other NSAIDs, have 3 or more alcoholic drinks a day, or take more or longer than directed.","Heart attack and stroke warning: NSAIDs, except aspirin, increase the risk of heart attack, heart failure and stroke.","Do not use right before or after heart surgery, or if you have had an allergic reaction to any other pain reliever or fever reducer.","Ask a doctor first if you have high blood pressure, heart disease, liver cirrhosis, kidney disease, asthma, a past stroke, stomach problems such as heartburn, or take a diuretic.","Ask a doctor or pharmacist first if you take aspirin for heart attack or stroke, or any other drug.","Stop use and ask a doctor if you see signs of stomach bleeding, heart or stroke symptoms, pain gets worse or lasts more than 10 days, or fever lasts more than 3 days.","If pregnant or breast-feeding, ask a health professional before use. It is especially important not to use ibuprofen at 20 weeks or later in pregnancy unless a doctor directs it.","Adults and children 12 and over: do not exceed 6 tablets in 24 hours unless directed by a doctor. Children under 12: ask a doctor."],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[{"url":"https://medlineplus.gov/periodpain.html","text":"MedlinePlus: Period Pain","summary":"Lists NSAIDs including ibuprofen and naproxen for period pain, who should avoid them, and when to see a provider."}]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=1a665e64-9f30-be37-4a83-38789f1f1e89","text":"DailyMed: Advil (ibuprofen) tablet label","summary":"Official Drug Facts: ibuprofen 200 mg, uses including menstrual cramps, full warnings and directions.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.target.com/p/advil-pain-reliever-fever-reducer-tablets-ibuprofen-nsaid/-/A-15772219","text":"Target: Advil Tablets (4.69/5, 12,462 reviews)","summary":"Retail listing with price, sizes and customer ratings."}]}}}'::jsonb),
  ('p-aleve-naproxen-220', 'Aleve Naproxen Sodium 220 mg Tablets', 'Aleve', 'medication', 'physical', 'Over-the-counter naproxen sodium 220 mg, a longer-acting NSAID. The label lists menstrual cramps among its uses. Adults take 1 tablet every 8 to 12 hours with a full glass of water (2 may be taken within the first hour for the first dose), and no more than 3 tablets in 24 hours.', '$14.99 for 50 tablets at Target', '', 'https://www.target.com/p/aleve-tablets-with-naproxen-sodium-220mg-nsaid-pain-reliever-fever-reducer-50-count/-/A-93719226', '["cramps","endometriosis","discomfort"]'::jsonb, '["cramp-relief"]'::jsonb, '["Target"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"FDA-regulated over-the-counter drug with a Drug Facts label (DailyMed, Bayer HealthCare LLC).","materials":"Oral tablet.","recalls":"No recalls found on the pages reviewed.","allergens":"Can cause severe allergic reactions, especially in people allergic to aspirin (hives, facial swelling, wheezing, shock, rash, blisters). Contains FD&C Blue #2 lake.","sideEffects":"Can cause severe stomach bleeding. The risk of heart attack or stroke may increase if you use more than directed or for longer than directed. Take with food or milk if it upsets your stomach.","opinionAlerts":"The label says it is especially important not to use naproxen sodium during the last 3 months of pregnancy unless definitely directed by a doctor."}'::jsonb, 'MedlinePlus lists NSAIDs such as naproxen for period pain, taken when symptoms start or when your period begins. Naproxen is dosed less often than ibuprofen, which some people find easier. The same cautions apply: avoid it with ulcers or other stomach problems, bleeding problems, liver disease or a true aspirin allergy, and see a clinician if cramps are severe, new after 25, or happen when you are not on your period. This is guidance about naproxen as a medicine, not a test of this brand.', 'Target shows a 4.8 out of 5 rating from 568 reviews for this Aleve 50-count listing.', 'Naproxen is one of the NSAIDs that clinical sources such as MedlinePlus recommend for menstrual cramps. Evidence is for the ingredient in general and does not validate this brand over generic naproxen sodium 220 mg.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of peer-reviewed literature and clinical guidance. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"communityReviewSourceUrl":"https://www.target.com/p/aleve-tablets-with-naproxen-sodium-220mg-nsaid-pain-reliever-fever-reducer-50-count/-/A-93719226","communityReviewSourceLabel":"Target reviews","ingredients":"Active: naproxen sodium 220 mg (naproxen 200 mg) (NSAID). Inactive: FD&C blue #2 lake, hypromellose, magnesium stearate, microcrystalline cellulose, polyethylene glycol, povidone, talc, titanium dioxide.","warnings":["Allergy alert: naproxen sodium may cause a severe allergic reaction, especially in people allergic to aspirin.","Stomach bleeding warning: risk is higher if you are 60 or older, have had ulcers or bleeding problems, take a blood thinner or steroid, take other NSAIDs, have 3 or more alcoholic drinks a day, or take more or longer than directed.","The risk of heart attack or stroke may increase if you use more than directed or for longer than directed.","Do not use right before or after heart surgery, or if you have had an allergic reaction to any other pain reliever or fever reducer.","Ask a doctor first if you have high blood pressure, heart disease, liver cirrhosis, kidney disease, asthma, stomach problems such as heartburn, or take a diuretic.","Stop use and ask a doctor if you see signs of stomach bleeding, have trouble swallowing, pain gets worse or lasts more than 10 days, or fever lasts more than 3 days.","If pregnant or breast-feeding, ask a health professional before use. It is especially important not to use naproxen sodium during the last 3 months of pregnancy unless definitely directed to do so by a doctor.","Adults and children 12 and over: do not exceed 2 tablets in any 8 to 12 hour period or 3 tablets in 24 hours. Children under 12: ask a doctor."],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[{"url":"https://medlineplus.gov/periodpain.html","text":"MedlinePlus: Period Pain","summary":"Lists NSAIDs including naproxen for period pain, who should avoid them, and when to see a provider."}]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=00ef5b30-71d0-4cb4-84a3-48c67d1cea2a","text":"DailyMed: Aleve (naproxen sodium) label, Bayer","summary":"Official Drug Facts: naproxen sodium 220 mg, uses including menstrual cramps, directions and inactive ingredients.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."},{"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=46e7b298-9e19-49b6-be71-e4fdcb09a5d4","text":"DailyMed: Aleve 220 mg label warnings","summary":"Full Aleve warning text, including the pregnancy warning about the last 3 months of pregnancy.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.target.com/p/aleve-tablets-with-naproxen-sodium-220mg-nsaid-pain-reliever-fever-reducer-50-count/-/A-93719226","text":"Target: Aleve 50 ct (4.8/5, 568 reviews)","summary":"Retail listing with price and customer ratings."}]}}}'::jsonb),
  ('p-monistat-3-combo', 'Monistat 3-Dose Yeast Infection Treatment (Prefilled Applicators + External Itch Cream)', 'Monistat', 'intimate-care', 'physical', 'A 3-night over-the-counter treatment for vaginal yeast infections. It comes with 3 prefilled applicators of miconazole nitrate 4% (200 mg each), used at bedtime 3 nights in a row, plus a tube of 2% miconazole cream for itching outside the vagina. For people who have had a yeast infection diagnosed by a doctor before.', '$15.89 at Target', 'https://target.scene7.com/is/image/Target/GUEST_17956779-2a01-4b05-a23d-33ae2edd3a56', 'https://www.target.com/p/monistat-3-dose-yeast-infection-treatment-3-prefilled-applicators-38-external-itch-cream-0-84oz/-/A-93324897', '["vaginal-health","discomfort"]'::jsonb, '["vaginal-health"]'::jsonb, '["Target"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"FDA-regulated over-the-counter drug with a Drug Facts label (DailyMed, Monistat 3 Combination Pack).","materials":"Prefilled vaginal cream applicators and an external cream tube.","recalls":"No recalls found on the pages reviewed.","allergens":"Inactive ingredients include propylene glycol, cetyl alcohol and stearyl alcohol. Stop and ask a doctor if you get a rash or hives.","sideEffects":"A mild increase in burning, itching or irritation may occur.","opinionAlerts":"The cream can damage condoms and diaphragms. Ask a doctor first if you take warfarin, since bleeding or bruising may occur."}'::jsonb, 'The CDC lists miconazole 4% cream for 3 days and miconazole 200 mg vaginal suppositories for 3 days among recommended over-the-counter options for uncomplicated vaginal yeast infections, and reports that azole treatment relieves symptoms in 80% to 90% of people who finish it. The CDC also notes that having had a yeast infection before does not make self-diagnosis reliable, so get checked if symptoms do not clear or come back within 2 months. In pregnancy, the CDC recommends only 7-day topical azole courses, so a 3-day product is not the pregnancy choice. This is guidance about miconazole, not a test of this brand.', 'Target shows a 4.21 out of 5 rating from 173 reviews for this Monistat 3 listing.', 'Miconazole is a CDC-recommended over-the-counter azole for uncomplicated vaginal yeast infections. Category-level evidence does not validate this brand over store-brand miconazole 3, which has the same active ingredient and strength.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of peer-reviewed literature and clinical guidance. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"communityReviewSourceUrl":"https://www.target.com/p/monistat-3-dose-yeast-infection-treatment-3-prefilled-applicators-38-external-itch-cream-0-84oz/-/A-93324897","communityReviewSourceLabel":"Target reviews","ingredients":"Active: miconazole nitrate 4% (200 mg per prefilled applicator); external cream miconazole nitrate 2%. Inactive (both creams): benzoic acid, cetyl alcohol, isopropyl myristate, polysorbate 60, potassium hydroxide, propylene glycol, purified water, stearyl alcohol.","warnings":["For vaginal use only. Do not use if you have never had a vaginal yeast infection diagnosed by a doctor.","Ask a doctor first if this is your first time with vaginal itching and discomfort; if you have lower abdominal, back or shoulder pain, fever, chills, nausea, vomiting or foul-smelling discharge; if you get yeast infections often (about once a month or 3 in 6 months); or if you may have been exposed to HIV.","Ask a doctor or pharmacist first if you take the prescription blood thinner warfarin, because bleeding or bruising may occur.","While using: do not use tampons, douches, spermicides or other vaginal products, and do not have vaginal intercourse. Condoms and diaphragms may be damaged.","Stop use and ask a doctor if symptoms do not improve in 3 days, last more than 7 days, or you get a rash, hives, abdominal pain, fever, chills, nausea, vomiting or foul-smelling discharge.","If pregnant or breast-feeding, ask a health professional before use.","Children under 12: ask a doctor."],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.cdc.gov/std/treatment-guidelines/candidiasis.htm","text":"CDC STI Treatment Guidelines: Vulvovaginal Candidiasis","summary":"Lists OTC miconazole and clotrimazole regimens, 80% to 90% response with azoles, when to seek testing, and 7-day topical azoles only in pregnancy."}]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/fda/fdaDrugXsl.cfm?setid=02c497e9-3b72-4dd2-83eb-a62b2eba1a9f&type=display","text":"DailyMed: Monistat 3 Combination Pack label","summary":"Official Drug Facts: miconazole nitrate 4% prefilled applicators and 2% external cream, warnings and directions.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.target.com/p/monistat-3-dose-yeast-infection-treatment-3-prefilled-applicators-38-external-itch-cream-0-84oz/-/A-93324897","text":"Target: Monistat 3-Dose (4.21/5, 173 reviews)","summary":"Retail listing with price and customer ratings."}]}}}'::jsonb),
  ('p-taro-clotrimazole-7', 'Taro Clotrimazole 1% 7-Day Vaginal Cream', 'Taro', 'intimate-care', 'physical', 'A low-cost 7-night over-the-counter treatment for vaginal yeast infections with clotrimazole 1%. Insert one applicatorful at bedtime for 7 days in a row; the same cream can be used on itchy skin outside the vagina twice a day for up to 7 days. For people who have had a yeast infection diagnosed by a doctor before.', '$6.29 for 1.5 oz (45 g) at Walmart', 'https://i5.walmartimages.com/seo/Taro-Clotrimazole-7-Vaginal-Cream-45-g_01c243f1-eccb-4843-9210-556e40650cb5.99099c95694f52d78d8c1c6a124feb83.jpeg', 'https://www.walmart.com/ip/Taro-Clotrimazole-7-Vaginal-Cream-45-g/46008111', '["vaginal-health","discomfort","cost"]'::jsonb, '["vaginal-health"]'::jsonb, '["Walmart"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"FDA-regulated over-the-counter drug with a Drug Facts label (DailyMed, clotrimazole vaginal cream USP 1%).","materials":"45 g tube of vaginal cream with a reusable applicator (wash after each use).","recalls":"No recalls found on the pages reviewed.","allergens":"Inactive ingredients include benzyl alcohol and cetostearyl alcohol. Stop and ask a doctor if you get a rash or hives.","sideEffects":"A mild increase in burning, itching or irritation may occur.","opinionAlerts":"The cream can damage condoms and diaphragms. A 7-day topical azole is the only type of yeast treatment the CDC recommends in pregnancy, but ask your prenatal clinician before using it."}'::jsonb, 'The CDC lists clotrimazole 1% cream, used daily for 7 to 14 days, as a recommended over-the-counter option for uncomplicated vaginal yeast infections, and notes azoles relieve symptoms in 80% to 90% of people who finish treatment. In pregnancy the CDC recommends only topical azoles used for 7 days, which makes a 7-day cream the relevant option to discuss with your prenatal clinician. Get checked if symptoms do not clear or return within 2 months. This is guidance about clotrimazole, not a test of this brand.', 'Walmart shows a 4.6 out of 5 rating from 223 ratings for this Taro Clotrimazole 7 listing.', 'Clotrimazole is a CDC-recommended over-the-counter azole for uncomplicated vaginal yeast infections. Category-level evidence does not validate this specific brand; other clotrimazole 1% 7-day creams contain the same active ingredient.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of peer-reviewed literature and clinical guidance. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"communityReviewSourceUrl":"https://www.walmart.com/ip/Taro-Clotrimazole-7-Vaginal-Cream-45-g/46008111","communityReviewSourceLabel":"Walmart reviews","ingredients":"Active: clotrimazole USP 1% (50 mg per applicatorful). Inactive: 2-octyldodecanol, benzyl alcohol, cetostearyl alcohol, cetyl esters wax, polysorbate 60, purified water, sorbitan monostearate.","warnings":["For vaginal use only. Do not use if you have never had a vaginal yeast infection diagnosed by a doctor.","Ask a doctor first if this is your first time with vaginal itching and discomfort; if you have lower abdominal, back or shoulder pain, fever, chills, nausea, vomiting or foul-smelling discharge; if you get yeast infections often (about once a month or 3 in 6 months); or if you may have been exposed to HIV.","While using: do not use tampons, douches, spermicides or other vaginal products, and do not have vaginal intercourse. Condoms and diaphragms may be damaged.","Stop use and ask a doctor if symptoms do not improve in 3 days, last more than 7 days, or you get a rash, hives, abdominal pain, fever, chills, nausea, vomiting or foul-smelling discharge.","If pregnant or breast-feeding, ask a health professional before use.","Children under 12: ask a doctor."],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.cdc.gov/std/treatment-guidelines/candidiasis.htm","text":"CDC STI Treatment Guidelines: Vulvovaginal Candidiasis","summary":"Lists clotrimazole 1% for 7 to 14 days as an OTC regimen and recommends only 7-day topical azoles in pregnancy."}]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=f7192955-8f8c-45dd-a215-8ac2c1f6444f","text":"DailyMed: Clotrimazole Vaginal Cream USP 1% (45 g) label","summary":"Official Drug Facts: clotrimazole 1%, 7-day directions, warnings and inactive ingredients.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.walmart.com/ip/Taro-Clotrimazole-7-Vaginal-Cream-45-g/46008111","text":"Walmart: Taro Clotrimazole 7 (4.6/5, 223 ratings)","summary":"Retail listing with price and customer ratings."}]}}}'::jsonb),
  ('p-womens-rogaine-foam', 'Women''s Rogaine 5% Minoxidil Foam', 'Rogaine', 'hair', 'physical', 'Unscented 5% minoxidil foam that regrows hair on the top of the scalp in women with hereditary thinning. Apply half a capful once a day to the thinning area. Results can show at about 3 months, some women need at least 6 months, and you have to keep using it to keep the regrowth.', '$58.65 at Target (2.11 oz cans; Target lists package quantity 2)', 'https://target.scene7.com/is/image/Target/GUEST_46c2cf3c-9fac-49cf-82eb-0bb182f66dc7', 'https://www.target.com/p/women-39-s-rogaine-5-minoxidil-foam-for-hair-thinning-and-loss-topical-treatment-for-hair-regrowth-2-11oz/-/A-16500199', '["hair","thinning","scalp","shedding"]'::jsonb, '["skin-hair"]'::jsonb, '["Target"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"FDA-regulated over-the-counter drug with a Drug Facts label (DailyMed, Women’s Rogaine Unscented). The AAD notes FDA has approved 2% and 5% minoxidil as a non-prescription treatment for women.","materials":"Aerosol foam. Extremely flammable: avoid fire, flame or smoking during and right after applying.","recalls":"No recalls found on the pages reviewed.","allergens":"No fragrance added (per Target). Contains SD alcohol 40-B, cetyl and stearyl alcohol, butylated hydroxytoluene, and propellants (butane, isobutane, propane).","sideEffects":"Scalp irritation or redness, unwanted facial hair, and changes in hair color or texture are possible. Stop and ask a doctor for chest pain, rapid heartbeat, faintness, dizziness, sudden weight gain, or swollen hands or feet.","opinionAlerts":"The label says it may be harmful if used when pregnant or breast-feeding. The AAD notes shedding can temporarily increase in the first 2 to 8 weeks."}'::jsonb, 'The American Academy of Dermatology describes minoxidil as an FDA-approved non-prescription treatment for female pattern hair loss. It takes about 6 to 12 months of continuous use to know how well it works for you, and the benefit is lost if you stop. Shedding can briefly increase in the first 2 to 8 weeks. Women who are pregnant, planning pregnancy or breastfeeding should avoid it. Sudden, patchy or postpartum hair loss is a different problem and worth a dermatologist visit. This is guidance about minoxidil, not a test of this brand.', 'Target shows a 3.91 out of 5 rating from 1,901 reviews for this Women''s Rogaine foam listing.', 'Minoxidil is the FDA-approved over-the-counter treatment for female pattern hair loss, per the AAD. The label notes regrowth varies and the product will not work for all women. Category-level evidence does not validate this brand over store-brand 5% minoxidil foam for women.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of peer-reviewed literature and clinical guidance. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"communityReviewSourceUrl":"https://www.target.com/p/women-39-s-rogaine-5-minoxidil-foam-for-hair-thinning-and-loss-topical-treatment-for-hair-regrowth-2-11oz/-/A-16500199","communityReviewSourceLabel":"Target reviews","ingredients":"Active: minoxidil 5% w/w (without propellant). Inactive: butane, butylated hydroxytoluene, cetyl alcohol, citric acid, glycerin, isobutane, lactic acid, polysorbate 60, propane, purified water, SD alcohol 40-B, stearyl alcohol.","warnings":["For external use only. Extremely flammable: avoid fire, flame or smoking during and right after application.","Do not use if your hair loss does not match the pattern on the carton, you have no family history of hair loss, your hair loss is sudden or patchy or linked to childbirth, you do not know the reason for it, you are under 18, your scalp is red, inflamed, infected, irritated or painful, or you use other medicines on the scalp.","Ask a doctor before use if you have heart disease.","Do not use more than directed or apply to other parts of the body. Avoid contact with eyes.","Stop use and ask a doctor if chest pain, rapid heartbeat, faintness or dizziness occurs; sudden unexplained weight gain occurs; hands or feet swell; scalp irritation or redness occurs; unwanted facial hair grows; or you see no regrowth after 6 months.","May be harmful if used when pregnant or breast-feeding."],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.aad.org/public/diseases/hair-loss/types/female-pattern","text":"AAD: Female pattern hair loss","summary":"Minoxidil is FDA-approved for women; use continuously 6 to 12 months to judge results; avoid in pregnancy and breastfeeding."}]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=4d328537-b7f5-43cc-9837-c5a0c6c390f8","text":"DailyMed: Women''s Rogaine Unscented foam label","summary":"Official Drug Facts: minoxidil 5% foam, who should not use it, warnings and directions.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.target.com/p/women-39-s-rogaine-5-minoxidil-foam-for-hair-thinning-and-loss-topical-treatment-for-hair-regrowth-2-11oz/-/A-16500199","text":"Target: Women''s Rogaine Foam (3.91/5, 1,901 reviews)","summary":"Retail listing with price and customer ratings."}]}}}'::jsonb),
  ('p-panoxyl-bpo-10-wash', 'PanOxyl 10% Benzoyl Peroxide Acne Foaming Wash', 'PanOxyl', 'skincare', 'physical', 'A 10% benzoyl peroxide acne wash for the face and body. Massage onto wet skin for 1 to 2 minutes, rinse, and start once a day, building to 2 or 3 times a day only if your skin tolerates it. It can bleach hair, towels and dyed fabrics.', '$9.89 for 5.5 oz at Target', 'https://target.scene7.com/is/image/Target/GUEST_99e7b206-1c38-49b8-9762-0c4533700929', 'https://www.target.com/p/panoxyl-maximum-strength-antimicrobial-acne-foaming-wash-for-face-chest-and-back-with-10-benzoyl-peroxide-unscented-5-5oz/-/A-14984165', '["acne","skin","pcos","cleanser"]'::jsonb, '["skin-hair"]'::jsonb, '["Target"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"FDA-regulated over-the-counter acne drug with a Drug Facts label (DailyMed, Crown Laboratories).","materials":"Foaming cream wash in a tube.","recalls":"No PanOxyl product appears on FDA''s March 2025 list of benzoyl peroxide acne products recalled for elevated benzene.","allergens":"Do not use if you have very sensitive skin or are sensitive to benzoyl peroxide.","sideEffects":"Dryness and irritation (redness, burning, itching, peeling or swelling) are possible, and more likely if you use another topical acne medicine at the same time.","opinionAlerts":"Bleaches hair and dyed fabrics. The AAD suggests storing benzoyl peroxide products at room temperature or cooler, replacing them every 10 to 12 weeks, and discarding any exposed to heat above about 78°F."}'::jsonb, 'The American Academy of Dermatology recommends benzoyl peroxide washes for blackheads, whiteheads, papules and pustules, and says to give treatment 6 to 8 weeks to work. FDA testing in 2025 found that most benzoyl peroxide acne products had undetectable or extremely low benzene, and a few recalled products did not include PanOxyl; the AAD advises storing these products cool and replacing them every 10 to 12 weeks. Hormonal or PCOS-related acne that does not respond is worth a clinician visit. This is guidance about benzoyl peroxide, not a test of this brand.', 'Target shows a 4.45 out of 5 rating from 1,694 reviews for this PanOxyl wash listing.', 'Benzoyl peroxide is an AAD-recommended over-the-counter acne ingredient. Category-level evidence does not validate this brand over other benzoyl peroxide washes; lower strengths may be gentler for sensitive skin.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of peer-reviewed literature and clinical guidance. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"communityReviewSourceUrl":"https://www.target.com/p/panoxyl-maximum-strength-antimicrobial-acne-foaming-wash-for-face-chest-and-back-with-10-benzoyl-peroxide-unscented-5-5oz/-/A-14984165","communityReviewSourceLabel":"Target reviews","ingredients":"Active: benzoyl peroxide 10%. Inactive: carbomer homopolymer type C, carbomer interpolymer type A, decyl glucoside, dimethicone, dioctyl sodium sulfosuccinate, glycerin, palmitic acid, polyacrylate crosspolymer-6, polyoxyl 40 stearate, propanediol, purified water, silica, sodium chloride, sodium citrate, sodium hydroxide, sodium laurylglucosides hydroxypropylsulfonate, sorbitan stearate, sorbitol, stearic acid, t-butyl alcohol, xanthan gum.","warnings":["For external use only.","Do not use if you have very sensitive skin or are sensitive to benzoyl peroxide.","Skin irritation and dryness are more likely if you use another topical acne medication at the same time. If irritation occurs, use only one topical acne medication at a time.","Avoid unnecessary sun exposure and use a sunscreen. Avoid contact with eyes, lips and mouth.","Avoid contact with hair and dyed fabrics, which may be bleached by this product.","Stop use and ask a doctor if irritation becomes severe.","If pregnant or breast-feeding, ask a health professional before use."],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.aad.org/public/diseases/acne/DIY/types-breakouts","text":"AAD: How to treat different types of acne","summary":"Recommends benzoyl peroxide washes for several acne types and 6 to 8 weeks to judge results."},{"url":"https://www.aad.org/news/benzoyl-peroxide-personal-care-products","text":"AAD statement on benzoyl peroxide products (March 2025)","summary":"Storage and replacement advice after FDA benzene testing; no immediate cause for concern."}]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=1660f219-e789-91f1-e063-6294a90a7664","text":"DailyMed: PanOxyl Acne Foaming Wash label","summary":"Official Drug Facts: benzoyl peroxide 10%, warnings, directions and inactive ingredients.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."},{"url":"https://www.fda.gov/drugs/drug-alerts-and-statements/limited-number-voluntary-recalls-initiated-after-fda-testing-acne-products-benzene-findings-show","text":"FDA: Benzene testing of acne products","summary":"FDA tested benzoyl peroxide acne products; a small number were recalled. PanOxyl is not on the recall list."}]},"community":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.target.com/p/panoxyl-maximum-strength-antimicrobial-acne-foaming-wash-for-face-chest-and-back-with-10-benzoyl-peroxide-unscented-5-5oz/-/A-14984165","text":"Target: PanOxyl 10% wash (4.45/5, 1,694 reviews)","summary":"Retail listing with price and customer ratings."}]}}}'::jsonb),
  ('p-differin-adapalene-gel', 'Differin Adapalene Gel 0.1% Acne Treatment', 'Differin', 'skincare', 'physical', 'Adapalene 0.1%, the one retinoid you can buy without a prescription. Apply a thin layer once a day over the whole acne-prone area on clean, dry skin. Acne may look worse in the first weeks, and full results can take up to 3 months.', '$23.99 for 45 g (1.6 oz) pump at Target', 'https://target.scene7.com/is/image/Target/GUEST_38a3ac7f-4dc8-4bf4-b9df-a38bb1e270a5', 'https://www.target.com/p/differin-adapalene-gel-with-pump-1-6oz/-/A-76545052', '["acne","skin","pcos","retinoid"]'::jsonb, '["skin-hair"]'::jsonb, '["Target"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"FDA-regulated over-the-counter drug (DailyMed lists it as a Human OTC Drug Label, Galderma Laboratories).","materials":"Gel in a pump bottle.","recalls":"No recalls found on the pages reviewed.","allergens":"Contains methylparaben and propylene glycol. Do not use if you are allergic to adapalene or any ingredient.","sideEffects":"Irritation is more likely in the first weeks or when combined with other topical acne medicines. Limit sun exposure and use sunscreen. Do not wax treated areas.","opinionAlerts":"The label says to ask a doctor before use if pregnant or breast-feeding, and to stop and ask a doctor if you become pregnant or plan to while using it."}'::jsonb, 'The American Academy of Dermatology notes that adapalene is the one retinoid available without a prescription and recommends a retinoid to help unclog pores in blackheads and whiteheads, giving treatment 6 to 8 weeks before judging it. Start slowly if your skin is sensitive, use sunscreen, and check with a clinician before using it if you are pregnant, trying to conceive or breastfeeding. This is guidance about adapalene, not a test of this brand.', 'Target shows a 4.36 out of 5 rating from 4,482 reviews for this Differin gel listing.', 'Adapalene is an over-the-counter retinoid recommended by the AAD for acne. The label says results may take up to 3 months. Category-level evidence does not validate this brand over generic adapalene 0.1% gel.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of peer-reviewed literature and clinical guidance. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"communityReviewSourceUrl":"https://www.target.com/p/differin-adapalene-gel-with-pump-1-6oz/-/A-76545052","communityReviewSourceLabel":"Target reviews","ingredients":"Active: adapalene 0.1% (retinoid). Inactive: carbomer 940, edetate disodium, methylparaben, poloxamer 182, propylene glycol, purified water, sodium hydroxide. May contain hydrochloric acid to adjust pH.","warnings":["For external use only.","Do not use on damaged skin (cuts, abrasions, eczema, sunburn) or if you are allergic to adapalene or any ingredient.","If pregnant or breast-feeding, ask a doctor before use.","Limit sun exposure and use sunscreen. Do not wax hair in treated areas. Avoid eyes, lips and mouth.","Acne may appear worse in the first few weeks, and irritation is more likely early on or with other topical acne medicines.","Stop use and ask a doctor if you become pregnant or plan to become pregnant while using it, have an allergic reaction, have severe irritation, or see no improvement after 3 months of daily use.","Apply once daily only. Children under 12: ask a doctor."],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.aad.org/public/diseases/acne/DIY/types-breakouts","text":"AAD: How to treat different types of acne","summary":"Notes adapalene is available without a prescription and recommends a retinoid for blackheads and whiteheads."}]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=0739d631-171b-42a8-bd55-0022b8df2d8a","text":"DailyMed: Differin (adapalene) gel OTC label","summary":"Official Drug Facts: adapalene 0.1%, pregnancy warnings, directions and inactive ingredients.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.target.com/p/differin-adapalene-gel-with-pump-1-6oz/-/A-76545052","text":"Target: Differin Gel 45 g (4.36/5, 4,482 reviews)","summary":"Retail listing with price and customer ratings."}]}}}'::jsonb),
  ('p-metamucil-psyllium-orange', 'Metamucil Psyllium Fiber Powder, Orange (with sugar)', 'Metamucil', 'supplement', 'physical', 'Psyllium husk fiber powder that you stir into at least 8 oz of liquid. Metamucil''s Drug Facts label for this canister lists it as fiber therapy for occasional constipation, usually working in 12 to 72 hours. Start with 1 dose a day and build up to 3 as needed, and always take it with enough fluid.', '$28.99 for 48.2 oz at Target', 'https://target.scene7.com/is/image/Target/GUEST_e38a4ac5-9e82-47dc-ba6a-c62be9537c9e', 'https://www.target.com/p/metamucil-psyllium-fiber-supplement-with-sugar-powder-orange-48-2oz/-/A-10988571', '["digestion","gut","bloating","supplement"]'::jsonb, '["supplement"]'::jsonb, '["Target"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Target''s listing shows Supplement Facts; Metamucil''s Drug Facts label for the orange smooth 48.2 oz canister (hosted on Target) lists psyllium husk as fiber therapy for regularity.","materials":"Powder in a canister.","recalls":"No recalls found on the pages reviewed.","allergens":"May cause an allergic reaction in people sensitive to inhaled or ingested psyllium. Contains FD&C Yellow No. 6.","sideEffects":"Taking it without enough fluid may cause it to swell and block your throat or esophagus (choking). The DailyMed Metamucil label notes bloating or changes in bowel habits may occur as you increase fiber.","opinionAlerts":"Contains added sugar (sucrose is the first ingredient). Take other medicines at least 2 hours before or after a dose."}'::jsonb, 'The NIH''s National Institute of Diabetes and Digestive and Kidney Diseases lists fiber supplements such as Metamucil among over-the-counter options for constipation, alongside eating more fiber (22 to 34 grams a day for adults), staying active, and drinking plenty of water and other liquids when you add fiber. A sudden change in bowel habits, rectal bleeding, or constipation lasting more than 7 days needs a clinician. This is guidance about fiber supplements in general, not a test of this brand over generic psyllium.', 'Target shows a 4.94 out of 5 rating from 43 reviews for this Metamucil 48.2 oz listing.', 'Fiber supplements are a recognized first-line over-the-counter option for occasional constipation per NIDDK. The label says it generally works in 12 to 72 hours. Category-level evidence does not validate this brand over store-brand psyllium.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of peer-reviewed literature and clinical guidance. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"communityReviewSourceUrl":"https://www.target.com/p/metamucil-psyllium-fiber-supplement-with-sugar-powder-orange-48-2oz/-/A-10988571","communityReviewSourceLabel":"Target reviews","ingredients":"Sucrose, psyllium husk, citric acid, natural and artificial orange flavor, Yellow 6 (per Target listing). Drug Facts: psyllium husk approx. 3.4 g per rounded tablespoon.","warnings":["Choking: taking this product without adequate fluid may cause it to swell and block your throat or esophagus. Do not take it if you have difficulty swallowing. Get immediate medical attention for chest pain, vomiting, or trouble swallowing or breathing after taking it.","Allergy alert: may cause an allergic reaction in people sensitive to inhaled or ingested psyllium.","Ask a doctor before use if you have a sudden change in bowel habits lasting 2 weeks, or abdominal pain, nausea or vomiting.","Take at least 2 hours before or after any prescription medicine taken by mouth.","Stop use and ask a doctor if constipation lasts more than 7 days or rectal bleeding occurs.","If pregnant or breast-feeding, ask a health professional before use (DailyMed Metamucil label).","Adults and children 12 and over: 1 rounded tablespoon in at least 8 oz of liquid, up to 3 times daily. Under 6: consult a doctor."],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/digestive-diseases/constipation/treatment","text":"NIDDK (NIH): Treatment for Constipation","summary":"Lists fiber supplements such as Metamucil among OTC options, with daily fiber and fluid advice."}]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://digitalcontent.target.com/vault/1768953600/CLOUD_b41b9e37-7484-43cb-8630-1d150a90e024.pdf","text":"Metamucil Therapy for Regularity Drug Facts (48.2 oz canister)","summary":"Psyllium husk 3.4 g per dose, choking and allergy warnings, and directions.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."},{"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=12d030b0-df97-4dd6-88ba-e9fe863c95ea","text":"DailyMed: Metamucil Therapy for Regularity label","summary":"Procter & Gamble Drug Facts for Metamucil psyllium powder, including pregnancy and medication-timing warnings.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.target.com/p/metamucil-psyllium-fiber-supplement-with-sugar-powder-orange-48-2oz/-/A-10988571","text":"Target: Metamucil 48.2 oz (4.94/5, 43 reviews)","summary":"Retail listing with price, Supplement Facts and customer ratings."}]}}}'::jsonb),
  ('p-miralax-peg-3350', 'MiraLAX Osmotic Laxative Powder, Unflavored', 'MiraLAX', 'gut-health', 'physical', 'Polyethylene glycol 3350, an unflavored osmotic laxative for occasional constipation. Stir one 17 g capful into 4 to 8 oz of any drink once a day; it usually works in 1 to 3 days. Do not use it for more than 7 days without talking to a doctor.', '$30.99 for 26.9 oz (45 doses) at Target', 'https://target.scene7.com/is/image/Target/GUEST_e144d80a-8509-4b9d-9c1c-e0ddb5c971d1', 'https://www.target.com/p/miralax-laxative-powder-45-days-26-9oz/-/A-14896180', '["digestion","gut","bloating"]'::jsonb, '["comfort"]'::jsonb, '["Target"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"FDA-regulated over-the-counter drug with a Drug Facts label (DailyMed, Bayer HealthCare LLC).","materials":"Powder in a bottle with a measuring cap.","recalls":"No recalls found on the pages reviewed.","allergens":"Do not use if you are allergic to polyethylene glycol. The label lists no inactive ingredients.","sideEffects":"Loose, watery or more frequent stools may occur. Stop and ask a doctor if you develop diarrhea, or bloating, cramping or abdominal pain gets worse.","opinionAlerts":"Do not use with kidney disease unless directed and supervised by a doctor. Do not mix with starch-based thickeners."}'::jsonb, 'NIDDK (NIH) lists osmotic agents such as MiraLAX among over-the-counter laxatives for constipation and notes a clinician may recommend a laxative for a short time, alongside more fiber, fluids and activity. Rectal bleeding, worsening pain, or needing a laxative for more than a week are reasons to see a clinician. This is guidance about osmotic laxatives in general, not a test of this brand over store-brand polyethylene glycol 3350.', 'Target shows a 4.63 out of 5 rating from 1,519 reviews for this MiraLAX 45-dose listing.', 'Polyethylene glycol 3350 is an osmotic laxative listed by NIDDK as an over-the-counter constipation option. The label says it generally produces a bowel movement in 1 to 3 days. Category-level evidence does not validate this brand over store-brand PEG 3350, which has the same active ingredient.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of peer-reviewed literature and clinical guidance. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"communityReviewSourceUrl":"https://www.target.com/p/miralax-laxative-powder-45-days-26-9oz/-/A-14896180","communityReviewSourceLabel":"Target reviews","ingredients":"Active: polyethylene glycol 3350, 17 g per dose. No inactive ingredients listed on the label.","warnings":["Allergy alert: do not use if you are allergic to polyethylene glycol.","Do not use if you have kidney disease, except under the advice and supervision of a doctor.","Ask a doctor before use if you have nausea, vomiting or abdominal pain; a sudden change in bowel habits lasting over 2 weeks; or irritable bowel syndrome.","Ask a doctor or pharmacist before use if you are taking a prescription drug.","Stop use and ask a doctor if you have rectal bleeding or your nausea, bloating, cramping or abdominal pain gets worse; you get diarrhea; or you need a laxative for more than 1 week.","If pregnant or breast-feeding, ask a health professional before use.","Adults and children 17 and over: once daily. Do not use for more than 7 days unless directed by a doctor. Children 16 and under: ask a doctor."],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.niddk.nih.gov/health-information/digestive-diseases/constipation/treatment","text":"NIDDK (NIH): Treatment for Constipation","summary":"Lists osmotic agents such as MiraLAX among OTC laxatives and notes short-term use on a clinician’s advice."}]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=d69ce3d4-7ca4-4fe3-b49e-6655e48d6963","text":"DailyMed: MiraLAX label","summary":"Official Drug Facts: polyethylene glycol 3350 17 g, warnings and directions.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.target.com/p/miralax-laxative-powder-45-days-26-9oz/-/A-14896180","text":"Target: MiraLAX 45 doses (4.63/5, 1,519 reviews)","summary":"Retail listing with price and customer ratings."}]}}}'::jsonb),
  ('p-nature-made-folic-acid-400', 'Nature Made Folic Acid 400 mcg Tablets', 'Nature Made', 'supplement', 'physical', 'One small tablet a day gives 400 mcg of folic acid (665 mcg DFE), the amount the CDC recommends daily for anyone who could become pregnant. USP Verified. Take 1 tablet daily with water and a meal.', '$6.59 for 250 tablets at Target', 'https://target.scene7.com/is/image/Target/GUEST_c1f5861a-74ef-4429-a9b2-bf0d8ba7446c', 'https://target.com/p/nature-made-folic-acid-400-mcg-665-mcg-dfe-tablets-250ct/-/A-11010058', '["pregnancy","fertility","supplement","cost"]'::jsonb, '["supplement","fertility"]'::jsonb, '["Target"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Dietary supplement (not FDA-approved). USP Verified for ingredients, potency and manufacturing, per Nature Made.","materials":"Oral tablet.","recalls":"No recalls found on the pages reviewed.","allergens":"Gluten free, no color added, no artificial flavors, no preservatives (per Nature Made).","sideEffects":"Nature Made advises keeping total daily folic acid from all sources at or below 1,000 mcg, since higher doses may mask a vitamin B12 shortfall.","opinionAlerts":"Check with a clinician if you take seizure medicines such as Dilantin or Mysoline. Nature Made marks this product discontinued on its own site, though Target still lists it."}'::jsonb, 'The CDC recommends that everyone who could become pregnant get 400 mcg of folic acid every day, starting at least 1 month before conception, because neural tube defects form in the first weeks of pregnancy, often before you know you are pregnant. The CDC notes folic acid is the only form of folate shown to help prevent neural tube defects. People who have had a pregnancy affected by a neural tube defect need a much higher dose and should talk with a doctor. This is guidance about folic acid, not a test of this brand.', 'Target shows a 4.6 out of 5 rating from 76 reviews for this Nature Made Folic Acid listing.', 'Daily folic acid before and in early pregnancy lowers the risk of neural tube defects, per the CDC, based on randomized trials. Evidence is for folic acid at 400 mcg and does not validate this brand over other USP-verified folic acid tablets.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of peer-reviewed literature and clinical guidance. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"communityReviewSourceUrl":"https://target.com/p/nature-made-folic-acid-400-mcg-665-mcg-dfe-tablets-250ct/-/A-11010058","communityReviewSourceLabel":"Target reviews","ingredients":"Folic acid 400 mcg (665 mcg DFE) per tablet. Other ingredients: cellulose gel, maltodextrin, croscarmellose sodium, stearic acid, magnesium stearate. Nature Made also lists 45 mg calcium per serving.","warnings":["Consult a healthcare professional if you take medications, especially seizure medications such as Dilantin or Mysoline (Nature Made).","Keep total daily folic acid from all sources at or below 1,000 mcg unless a clinician advises otherwise (Nature Made).","If you have had a pregnancy affected by a neural tube defect, talk with a doctor about the higher dose the CDC recommends."],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.cdc.gov/folic-acid/about/index.html","text":"CDC: About Folic Acid","summary":"400 mcg daily for anyone who could become pregnant, starting at least 1 month before conception; folic acid is the form shown to prevent neural tube defects."}]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.naturemade.com/products/nature-made-folic-acid-tablets","text":"Nature Made: Folic Acid 400 mcg","summary":"Brand page with supplement facts, USP Verified status, and interaction notes. Marked discontinued on the brand site.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"url":"https://target.com/p/nature-made-folic-acid-400-mcg-665-mcg-dfe-tablets-250ct/-/A-11010058","text":"Target: Nature Made Folic Acid 250 ct (4.6/5, 76 reviews)","summary":"Retail listing with price, ingredients and customer ratings."}]}}}'::jsonb),
  ('p-easyhome-lh-strips-50', 'Easy@Home Ovulation Test Strips (50 LH Tests)', 'Easy@Home', 'diagnostics', 'physical', 'A budget pack of 50 plain urine LH strips that show when your luteinizing hormone surges, which usually comes shortly before ovulation. Dip, wait 3 to 5 minutes, and read the lines. Results can be logged in the Premom app.', '$16.99 for 50 strips at Walmart', 'https://i5.walmartimages.com/seo/Easy-Home-Reliable-Ovulation-Predictor-Kit-50-LH-Tests-50-Count_97181863-097f-4d20-8305-1f27d899d7e1.f07b15b47e10c12116db2df39dc6a3a8.jpeg', 'https://www.walmart.com/ip/Easy-Home-50-Ovulation-Test-Strips-Kit-the-Reliable-Ovulation-Predictor-Kit-50-LH-Test/407693487', '["fertility","cost","privacy"]'::jsonb, '["fertility","cycle-tracking"]'::jsonb, '["Walmart"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"FDA clearance status is not stated on the Walmart listing.","materials":"Urine test strips (5 mm wide).","recalls":"No recalls found on the pages reviewed.","allergens":"N/A (external, urine dip test).","sideEffects":"None; this is a urine test.","opinionAlerts":"The FDA says not to use ovulation tests to prevent pregnancy. MedlinePlus notes birth control pills, hormone therapy and clomiphene can change LH levels, and irregular cycles can make a surge hard to catch."}'::jsonb, 'The FDA explains that urine ovulation tests detect the LH surge that happens about 1 to 1.5 days before ovulation and are reliable about 9 times out of 10 when used carefully and started at the right point in your cycle. MedlinePlus suggests starting 3 to 5 days before you expect to ovulate (around day 11 of a 28-day cycle) and avoiding large amounts of fluid before testing. They are not birth control. If you cannot detect a surge or are not pregnant after several months, talk with a clinician. This is guidance about LH tests in general, not a test of this brand.', 'Walmart shows a 4.6 out of 5 rating from 75 ratings for this Easy@Home 50-strip listing.', 'FDA describes urine LH tests as detecting the LH surge about 9 times in 10 when used correctly. The Walmart listing gives no accuracy or sensitivity data for these specific strips, so that figure is category-level only.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of peer-reviewed literature and clinical guidance. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"communityReviewSourceUrl":"https://www.walmart.com/ip/Easy-Home-50-Ovulation-Test-Strips-Kit-the-Reliable-Ovulation-Predictor-Kit-50-LH-Test/407693487","communityReviewSourceLabel":"Walmart reviews","ingredients":"50 individually wrapped LH urine test strips (the listing does not state the LH sensitivity threshold).","warnings":["Do not use ovulation tests to prevent pregnancy; they are not reliable for that purpose (FDA).","Start testing at the right time in your cycle or results will be unreliable (FDA).","Hormonal birth control, hormone therapy and clomiphene can affect LH levels; irregular cycles can make a surge hard to detect (MedlinePlus)."],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[{"url":"https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/007062.htm","text":"MedlinePlus: Ovulation home test","summary":"When to start testing, what a positive means, and what can affect results."}]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.fda.gov/medical-devices/home-use-tests/ovulation-urine-test","text":"FDA: Ovulation (Urine Test)","summary":"LH surge about 1 to 1.5 days before ovulation; reliable about 9 times in 10; not for preventing pregnancy.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.walmart.com/ip/Easy-Home-50-Ovulation-Test-Strips-Kit-the-Reliable-Ovulation-Predictor-Kit-50-LH-Test/407693487","text":"Walmart: Easy@Home 50 LH strips (4.6/5, 75 ratings)","summary":"Retail listing with price and customer ratings."}]}}}'::jsonb),
  ('p-visby-womens-sti-test', 'Visby Women''s At-Home STI Test', 'Visby Medical', 'diagnostics', 'physical', 'The first FDA-authorized test for chlamydia, gonorrhea and trichomoniasis that you can buy without a prescription and run entirely at home. You collect a vaginal swab, a single-use PCR device runs the test, and results show in the Visby app in about 30 minutes. Visby includes a same-day telehealth visit if you test positive; medication cost is not included.', '$149.99 on visby.com (listed as a sale from $179.99)', '', 'https://visby.com/products/visby-womens-at-home-sti-test-kit', '["privacy","vaginal-health"]'::jsonb, '["sexual-health"]'::jsonb, '["Visby.com"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"FDA De Novo marketing authorization (March 28, 2025) as the first home test for chlamydia, gonorrhea and trichomoniasis, sold without a prescription.","materials":"Single-use powered PCR test device, swab with buffer vial, and power adapter. Requires the Visby Medical app.","recalls":"No recalls found on the pages reviewed.","allergens":"N/A (self-collected vaginal swab).","sideEffects":"None expected from swab collection. The main risk is a false positive or false negative result.","opinionAlerts":"Tests for only 3 infections. Visby lists it for ages 14 and up and U.S. only; telehealth and delivery are available only in select areas."}'::jsonb, 'The CDC recommends yearly chlamydia screening for all sexually active women under 25, and for older women at higher risk, because infection is often silent and can lead to pelvic inflammatory disease, ectopic pregnancy and infertility. The FDA authorized this test after studies in which it correctly identified about 97% to 100% of positive and about 98.5% to 99% of negative samples, but it warns that false results can happen. Anyone who tests positive should get care, and anyone with symptoms or a recent exposure should still see a clinician after a negative result. This test does not check for HIV, syphilis or other STIs.', null, 'In FDA''s review, the test correctly identified 98.8% of negative and 97.2% of positive chlamydia samples, 99.1% of negative and 100% of positive gonorrhea samples, and 98.5% of negative and 97.8% of positive trichomoniasis samples. These are the FDA-reported study results for this specific device.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of peer-reviewed literature and clinical guidance. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"ingredients":"Single-use PCR device, vaginal swab with buffer vial, power adapter (per Visby).","warnings":["False negative results can delay treatment and allow infection to spread (FDA).","Seek medical care after a positive result. If you have symptoms, a recent exposure or other concerns, contact a clinician even after a negative result (FDA).","Tests only for chlamydia, gonorrhea and trichomoniasis."],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.cdc.gov/std/treatment-guidelines/chlamydia.htm","text":"CDC STI Treatment Guidelines: Chlamydial Infections","summary":"Annual screening for sexually active women under 25 and older women at increased risk; untreated infection can cause PID, ectopic pregnancy and infertility."}]},"scientific":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.fda.gov/news-events/press-announcements/fda-grants-marketing-authorization-first-home-test-chlamydia-gonorrhea-and-trichomoniasis","text":"FDA: First home test for chlamydia, gonorrhea and trichomoniasis","summary":"March 2025 De Novo authorization of the Visby Medical Women’s Sexual Health Test, with accuracy data and limitations.","justification":"Conservative ayna classification: category or adjacent evidence only; this source does not validate this specific product."}]},"community":{"links":[{"url":"https://visby.com/products/visby-womens-at-home-sti-test-kit","text":"Visby: Women''s At-Home STI Test Kit","summary":"Brand product page with price, kit contents, age range and telehealth details."}]}}}'::jsonb),
  ('p-rugby-vitamin-b6-25', 'Rugby Vitamin B6 25 mg Tablets', 'Rugby', 'supplement', 'physical', 'Plain vitamin B6 (pyridoxine HCl) 25 mg tablets. The 25 mg strength matches the dose range ACOG recommends for nausea and vomiting of pregnancy, but how often to take it should come from your prenatal clinician.', '$8.11 for 100 tablets at Target (sold by a third-party seller)', 'https://target.scene7.com/is/image/Target/GUEST_82e8093d-18ff-416c-8cc1-df4e6c2b314e', 'https://www.target.com/p/rugby-vitamin-b6-25mg-tablets-100ct/-/A-1006726140', '["pregnancy","supplement","cost"]'::jsonb, '["supplement"]'::jsonb, '["Target"]'::jsonb, '{}'::jsonb, '{"fdaStatus":"Dietary supplement (not FDA-approved).","materials":"Oral tablet.","recalls":"No recalls found on the pages reviewed.","allergens":"Other ingredients: microcrystalline cellulose, dicalcium phosphate, stearic acid, talc, croscarmellose sodium, magnesium stearate, hypromellose.","sideEffects":"NIH ODS notes very high long-term B6 intakes can cause nerve damage (sensory neuropathy). The adult upper limit is 100 mg a day, including in pregnancy, unless a clinician is supervising treatment.","opinionAlerts":"ACOG’s dosing (10 to 25 mg three or four times a day) can reach the 100 mg daily upper limit, so NIH ODS advises pregnant women to consult a physician before taking B6. Sold by a third-party seller on Target."}'::jsonb, 'According to the NIH Office of Dietary Supplements, ACOG recommends vitamin B6 alone, 10 to 25 mg three or four times a day, as a first treatment for nausea and vomiting of pregnancy, adding doxylamine if that is not enough. Two placebo-controlled trials found 30 to 75 mg a day reduced nausea, while a Cochrane review could not draw firm conclusions. Because these doses can approach the 100 mg daily upper limit, check with your prenatal clinician first, and seek care right away for vomiting that keeps you from holding down fluids. This is guidance about vitamin B6, not a test of this brand.', null, 'Evidence for B6 alone in pregnancy nausea is mixed: two placebo-controlled trials showed less nausea at 30 to 75 mg a day, and a Cochrane review was inconclusive (NIH ODS). B6 combined with doxylamine has stronger trial support. Evidence is category-level and does not validate this brand.', 'independent', 'ayna synthesis of peer-reviewed literature and clinical guidance. Not a direct clinician quote.', 'curated', false, false, null, true, '{"ingredients":"Vitamin B6 (as pyridoxine HCl) 25 mg per tablet. Other ingredients: microcrystalline cellulose, dicalcium phosphate, stearic acid, talc, croscarmellose sodium, magnesium stearate, hypromellose.","warnings":["Keep out of reach of children. Do not use if the seal under the cap is broken or missing (label, via Target).","Pregnant women should consult a physician before taking vitamin B6 supplements, since treatment doses can approach the 100 mg daily upper limit (NIH ODS).","Chronic very high doses can cause severe, progressive sensory neuropathy (NIH ODS)."],"verificationLinks":{"doctor":{"links":[{"url":"https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/VitaminB6-HealthProfessional/","text":"NIH ODS: Vitamin B6 Health Professional Fact Sheet","summary":"Reports ACOG’s recommendation of 10 to 25 mg B6 three or four times daily for pregnancy nausea, mixed trial evidence, and the 100 mg upper limit."}]},"scientific":{"links":[]},"community":{"links":[{"url":"https://www.target.com/p/rugby-vitamin-b6-25mg-tablets-100ct/-/A-1006726140","text":"Target: Rugby Vitamin B6 25 mg, 100 ct","summary":"Retail listing with price and Supplement Facts. No reviews yet."}]}}}'::jsonb)
on conflict (id) do nothing;

